OL,3,GNEWSACosts force cat cafe to lose
OL,4,Afelines to stay open
OL,5,
OL,6,FA self-confessed "crazy cat lady" who
OL,7,Fopened a cat cafe three years ago said
OL,8,Frising costs had forced her decision to
OL,9,Fkeep the coffee shop, but without the
OL,10,Ffurry felines.
OL,12,FShelley Smith opened Finnegan's
OL,13,FWhiskers in North Street in Sudbury,
OL,14,FSuffolk, where for years visitors have
OL,15,Fbeen able to book to come in, enjoy a
OL,16,Fcoffee and play with the resident cats.
OL,18,FHowever, Smith said she had to make the
OL,19,F"heartbreaking" decision to rebrand -
OL,20,Fminus the cats - because "we're not
OL,21,Fgetting enough people through the door
OL,22,Fto make it financially viable, sadly".
